# Trivy config accepted risks — Group 9
# Format: rule id. Justification — owner — expires YYYY-MM-DD
# Reviewed 2026-09-30 (G5): both still hold; renewed with the reasons below.

# The internal ALB speaks HTTP to the tasks. It is not reachable from the internet: only API
# Gateway's VPC link and tasks inside the VPC reach it, and TLS ends at API Gateway. HTTPS on the ALB
# needs a certificate for a private name; revisit with a custom domain.
# AVD-AWS-0054 — HTTP listener on internal ALB — @emebetgirmay — expires 2026-12-31
AVD-AWS-0054

# Tasks (POS, Payments, Commission, k6, DB bootstrap) and the in-VPC Lambda need HTTPS out through
# the NAT gateway for ECR, Secrets Manager, CloudWatch Logs and X-Ray. Interface VPC endpoints
# instead would cost about $92 a month against the NAT's $34 (docs/cost-model.md).
# AVD-AWS-0104 — ECS task egress 443 — @emebetgirmay — expires 2026-12-31
AVD-AWS-0104

# Alias used by some Trivy builds for the same egress check:
aws-vpc-no-public-egress-sgr
